  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Θ -Categories and Tannakian duality — We introduce a notion of Θ-categories, which is a refinement of the notion of symmetric monoidal ∞-categories.\n\n**Θ -Categories and Tannakian duality**\n\n*Joost NUITEN, Bertrand TOEN*\n\n33 pp, 9 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We introduce a notion of Θ-categories, which is a refinement of the notion of symmetric monoidal ∞-categories. We use this notion to prove a Tannakian duality statement, relating Θ-categories with fpqc- stacks by means of a certain stack of fiber functors in the context of Θ-categories. This provides, over a base ring of arbitrary characteris- tic, a strong link between Tannakian Θ-categories and the schematic homotopy types of [Toe06].\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; -Categories; -Categories; -Categories of modules; Tannaka duality; -Categories of quasi-coherent and ind-perfect ; Tannakian -categories and Tannakian gerbes; The Tannakian duality theorem; Positive tor-dimension descent",
      "lang": "en",
